&lt;h3&gt;About &lt;a href="http://customer.io/"&gt;Customer.io&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Over 9,000 companies — from scrappy startups to global brands — use our platform to send billions of emails, push notifications, in-app messages, and SMS every day. &lt;a href="http://Customer.io"&gt;Customer.io&lt;/a&gt; powers automated communication that people actually want to receive. We help teams send smarter, more relevant messages using real-time behavioral data.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;About the role&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Hi, my name is Megan Berry, Senior Director of Product at &lt;a href="http://customer.io/"&gt;Customer.io&lt;/a&gt;, and I'm looking for a Senior Product Manager to help us turn customer signals into products people actually want.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Our team is six product managers who partner closely with Design and Engineering to launch first-class products that drive customer and business outcomes. You need to be able to synthesize customer research, market research, analytics and your own taste into a customer-first roadmap and set of releases. You will work with a cross-functional team with a high level of autonomy to validate ideas early and help the team ship excellent work. This role focuses on Workflows.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;What we value&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Surfacing customer problems based on qualitative and quantitative data.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Driving alignment through effective communication.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Performing market research and presenting findings.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Using AI to accelerate discovery.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Helping our teams ship sooner.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;What you’ll do&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Identify and validate customer problems through user research, usage analytics, partner insights, and AI-powered discovery tools.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Rapidly prototype and run focused experiments to test hypotheses and de-risk new ideas early in development.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead cross-functional planning by aligning Engineering, Design, and business stakeholders around clear product goals and trade-offs.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Drive feature strategy and influence roadmaps by proposing initiatives rooted in customer impact and market opportunity.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Break down complex projects into incremental, testable releases, using component reuse and system thinking to accelerate delivery.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Define product success metrics upfront and track adoption, engagement, and retention to inform iterative improvement.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Take on Technology Lead responsibilities for specific initiatives when needed, including data analysis, prototyping, coordinating engineering work, and managing delivery risks.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Look at product metrics after launch and work with GTM stakeholders to ensure your launches are successful and create the product and business outcomes we want.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;What we're looking for&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;7+ years of product management experience, ideally including time in B2B SaaS or platforms that leverage behavioral data for automation or messaging.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong analytical skills, comfort with metrics dashboards, and experience using data to shape direction and evaluate impact.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proven ability to lead feature development independently, reduce scope, and deliver successful outcomes with tight teams.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;High product intuition balanced with humility and experimentation. You're comfortable being wrong and eager to learn quickly.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Exceptional written communication and decision-framing abilities, especially in remote and async-first environments.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ex

